        // ...
        mClickedFilter = true;  // Set asynchronously!
    }
});
```

When the user presses the right arrow button, the `nextImg()` method checks:
```java
if (mClicked == mClickedFilter) {  // true == false → toast shown!
    next();
} else
    Toast.makeText(..., R.string.save_first, ...).show();
```

Since `mClickedFilter` is still `false` (the async save hasn't completed yet), the condition `mClicked == mClickedFilter` evaluates to `false`, incorrectly showing the "Save first" toast even though the image was saved.

**Fix:** Set `mClickedFilter = true` in `saveC()` **before** calling `saveCurrentImage()`, so it's set synchronously when the user commits to saving.

